WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.910
Grab a hand pump and pump
air hard into a flat ball,

2
00:00:03.960 --> 00:00:06.090
stroke after stroke.

3
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.650
Each stroke squeezes the air in
quickly, and its temperature rises.

4
00:00:10.700 --> 00:00:14.030
A warmer gas has faster random
motion of its particles,

5
00:00:14.080 --> 00:00:16.390
so more internal energy.

6
00:00:16.440 --> 00:00:18.880
So where did that energy come from?

7
00:00:18.930 --> 00:00:20.470
Was the air heated?

8
00:00:20.520 --> 00:00:24.730
In this mission, you'll pin down
exactly what heating means in physics.

9
00:00:24.780 --> 00:00:28.170
Then you'll find out why, in an ideal gas,

10
00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:31.970
internal energy is all
random kinetic energy.

11
00:00:32.020 --> 00:00:34.950
Your mission: decide
whether the air was heated,

12
00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:36.360
and explain your answer.
